        "payload": "tree c3cf002c3cbdd957f4c574b852e80da6585f4d99\nparent 7988380da987c0b860885853ace8149b84ac2ee8\nauthor Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1790896506 +0200\ncommitter Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1790897213 +0200\n\nsign: use fresh randomness as BIP340 auxiliary data\n\nMutableTransactionSignatureCreator::CreateSchnorrSig passed all-zero\nauxiliary data to SignSchnorr. BIP340 recommends fresh randomness there,\nfor protection against fault injection and side-channel attacks. Pass\nGetRandHash() instead.\n\nThe BIP341 key path vectors were generated with zero auxiliary data, so\nthe test no longer compares the creator's signature byte for byte. It\nnow checks that two signatures differ and are both valid, and\nreproduces the vector signature by calling SignSchnorr with zero\nauxiliary data.\n\nThe script_sign fuzz target can now reach GetRandHash() through\nSignTransaction, so it seeds the global RNG like the other signing\ntargets.\n",
